# Backend for iOS (mandatory scope)

When the user asks for **iOS backend**, **mobile API**, or **API for the app**, work only on what native clients need over HTTP JSON.

## Edit here

| Area | Paths |
|------|--------|
| Mobile route handlers | `backend/main.py` (mobile sections) — prefer grouping changes; long-term home is `backend/mobile/` |
| Mobile contract & index | `backend/mobile/contract.py`, `backend/mobile/README.md` |
| Serialization shared with grid | `backend/utils/car_serialize.py`, `backend/db/inventory_db.py` (only if iOS payload needs it) |
| Geo / search / dealers for app | `backend/listings/geo_session.py`, `backend/listings/dealer_locator.py`, `backend/utils/hybrid_search.py` |
| Auth session (mobile) | `backend/login.py` patterns, `backend/utils/csrf.py`, `backend/db/users_db.py` (minimal) |
| Tests | `backend/tests/test_mobile_*.py`, `backend/tests/test_car_detail_api.py`, `backend/tests/test_saved_cars_api.py`, `backend/tests/test_listings_perf.py` (API-only) |
| Contract (client) | `ios/docs/API_CONTRACT.md` — update when routes or shapes change |
| Security | `docs/SECURITY_MASTER_TODO.md` — SEC-011, SEC-013, SEC-077, SEC-040, etc. |

## Do not edit (iOS-backend tasks)

- `frontend/templates/`, `frontend/static/` — website markup and JS
- `backend/listings/routes.py` HTML `listings_page` unless a shared helper is required for JSON parity
- Scanners, dev console, dealer portal, OEM pipelines, vector reindex — unless the user explicitly ties them to a mobile API

## Delivery checklist

1. Match request/response shapes expected by `ios/SarrafiCars/SarrafiCars/Networking/` (`APIClient.swift`, `Models.swift`).
2. Update `ios/docs/API_CONTRACT.md` and `backend/mobile/contract.py` for new or changed routes.
3. Add or extend tests under `backend/tests/test_mobile_*.py`.
4. Re-run **Validation** for touched SEC rows; update **Last verified** and **Changelog** in `docs/SECURITY_MASTER_TODO.md`.

## Parity rule

Website and iOS may share endpoints (e.g. `GET /api/listings/cars`). Prefer **one implementation** used by both. Do not duplicate business logic in `frontend/static/` for behavior the app needs from the server.
